&lt;i&gt;Ms. Frag&lt;/i&gt;. 32—and demonstrates that the recycled manuscript copies are rare and unique witnesses for the texts they originally contained.</note></biblStruct><bibl type="formatted" subtype="bibliography" resp="https://www.zotero.org/styles/chicago-note-bibliography-17th-edition">
